---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PaletteStack from "../../components/PaletteStack.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1>Colors</h1>
  <p>This design system comes with a bunch of colors of different luminosity level and hue.</p>

  <PaletteStack
    palettes={["red", "orange", "yellow", "green", "cyan", "blue", "purple", "teal", "gray"]}
  />

  <p>There are also additional palettes for some brand colors.</p>

  <PaletteStack palettes={["makigas", "ngl"]} />

  <p>
    To compose either of these colors, use a CSS variable with the following structure: <code>
      --genshi-<var>palette</var>-<var>lum</var>
    </code>. Some examples:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><code>--genshi-red-400</code></li>
    <li><code>--genshi-blue-900</code></li>
    <li><code>--genshi-makigas-500</code></li>
  </ul>
</Layout>
